# AgentGate — resume block opening (example, not an active override)
#
# HOW THIS FILE IS READ
#   - This file is named .example, so it is NOT loaded. Copy it to
#     `prompts/resume.md` to make it active.
#   - Leading `#` comment lines are stripped and never sent to the model.
#   - The section heading ("## Resuming an existing session") is added by
#     AgentGate, not by this file. Do not add it here; it will be duplicated.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
#   Only the opening lines of the resume block are overridable. The workspace
#   path, the history file path, the format description, and the last-two-turn
#   digest are appended automatically and are not configurable here.
#
# PREFIX-CACHE RULE — please preserve it when editing
#   The resume block sits after the stable base rules and before per-session
#   memory, so it must stay identical for the life of a session. Do not add
#   timestamps, turn counters, or anything that changes between turns.

